---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Support · AutoLog"
  description="Adapters, K-line patience, and where your data lives. Six questions, answered straight."
>
  <div class="page-column">
    <div class="head">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="sub">Six questions, answered straight.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Which adapters work?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          Any BLE ELM327 adapter, usually about $15. Classic Bluetooth and
          WiFi-only adapters cannot be used. iOS gives apps no path to them.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span class="q"
            >Why does the first connection to an older car take a while?</span
          >
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          Older cars talk on the K-line, ISO 9141-2, and the protocol search
          is slow by design. The adapter tries each protocol in turn until
          the car answers. The 2002 Miata in the test fleet takes its time
          too. Give the first connection half a minute; the ones after are
          quicker.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Does it clear codes?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          No. Ever. AutoLog reads live data and reports the faults it sees.
          It never clears a code and never writes anything to the car.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Does it work with EVs and hybrids?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          Yes. The app watches which signals the car actually answers and
          builds the cockpit from those. A hybrid keeps its engine-off miles;
          an EV gets gauges without fuel math.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Will it drain the car battery?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          The adapter draws a small idle current from the port; the app
          itself takes nothing from the car. Weeks of parking are fine. If
          the car sits for a season, unplug the adapter.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Where does my data live?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          On the phone, in full. No account, no server, no analytics. Two
          lookups leave the device: a VIN decode and road geometry from
          OpenStreetMap. The privacy page lists both.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="panel contact">
      <p class="contact-line">Still stuck? Write to the engineer.</p>
      <!-- TODO: dedicated address -->
      <p class="contact-email">hello@&hellip;</p>
    </div>

    <p class="build-marker">TESTFLIGHT BUILD 12</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 100px 24px 40px;
  }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-bottom: 44px;
  }

  .head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 44px;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .sub {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .faq {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 22px 26px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-amber);
    outline-offset: -2px;
    border-radius: var(--panel-radius);
  }

  .faq-item .q {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.92);
  }

  .faq-item .a {
    padding: 0 60px 26px 26px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 24px;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.6);
  }

  .caret {
    position: relative;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .caret::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: auto;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-right: 1.5px solid var(--text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--text-muted);
    transform: translateY(-2px) rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.2s var(--ease-spring);
  }

  details[open] .caret::before {
    transform: translateY(1px) rotate(225deg);
  }

  .contact {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: 36px;
    padding: 26px;
    border-color: rgba(200, 127, 60, 0.35);
  }

  .contact-line {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.92);
  }

  .contact-email {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .build-marker {
    padding: 72px 0 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-column {
      padding: 64px 24px 30px;
    }

    .head {
      gap: 10px;
      padding-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .head h1 {
      font-size: 34px;
    }

    .sub {
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    .faq {
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .faq-item summary {
      padding: 18px 20px;
    }

    .faq-item .q {
      font-size: 15.5px;
      line-height: 22px;
    }

    .faq-item .a {
      padding: 0 20px 20px;
      font-size: 14.5px;
      line-height: 23px;
    }

    .contact {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 28px;
      padding: 22px 20px;
    }

    .contact-line {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .build-marker {
      padding: 56px 0 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
